I suspect one additional issue

Your node is Ready, but the Machine Config Operator Deployment is Pending.

On an SNO cluster, those deployments normally schedule on the master node.

A very common cause is that the node has insufficient allocatable resources after enabling the RT kernel or PerformanceProfile, or there are strict CPU pinning/topology constraints preventing the pods from scheduling.

The output of:

oc describe pod -n openshift-machine-config-operator machine-config-operator-659c6fb5db-lfw27

will confirm the exact reason within a few lines, usually under Events (for example, "Insufficient cpu", "node(s) didn't match PodTopologySpread", "untolerated taint", etc.).

From everything you've shared so far, the MCP itself is not broken anymore—the remaining problem is almost certainly that the machine-config-operator and machine-config-controller pods are stuck in Pending, preventing the MCP status from being reconciled.
